{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inner-honourable-bluejay","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`pytest_sessionfinish`'s working-tree backstop in `tests/conftest.py` prints:\n\n    \"REPO ISOLATION FAILURE: the test run left new changes in the checkout \"\n    \"(a test wrote into the working tree instead of tmp_path). Offending entries ...\"\n\nIt is the third member of the shared-checkout guard family, and it makes the same causal\nclaim its two siblings have now had corrected. Its only evidence is two\n`git status --porcelain` snapshots taken around the whole session, so \"a test wrote into the\nworking tree\" is exactly the attribution a snapshot diff cannot supply — a concurrent commit,\nrebase, branch switch, or editor save by another process in the same checkout produces an\nidentical diff. `docs/local-dev-env.md` (lines 425-450) already documents that these guards\nmisfire that way.\n\nMilder than its siblings: it prescribes NO destructive remedy, so nothing here can destroy a\ndeveloper's work. The defect is confined to the false causal claim and to the word \"Offending\".\n\n## Prior art\n\n- `tests/_isolation.py::leak_failure_message`, corrected under `746c-185a-0e48-4b83`.\n- `tests/_isolation.py::head_move_failure_message`, corrected under `a991-09dd-aa6a-4a27`\n  (which is where this was found; the HEAD-move guard's remedy was the dangerous case and was\n  fixed first, keeping that change tight).\n\nBoth extract the text into `tests/_isolation.py` so it can be pinned on observable content.\nThe same treatment applies: name the concurrent-external possibility instead of asserting the\none cause the backstop cannot know, and pin it alongside the existing assertions in\n`tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py`.\n\n## Scope\n\nWording only. The backstop must keep failing the run exactly as it does now (it still escalates\n`session.exitstatus` so CI catches a genuine leak) — this is not a weakening of detection.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The backstop message no longer asserts that a test made the change; it names the\n      concurrent-external cause, mirroring `leak_failure_message`.\n- [ ] The text lives in `tests/_isolation.py` so it is assertable on observable content.\n- [ ] A test pins the property alongside the existing ones in\n      `tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py`.\n- [ ] The backstop still sets `session.exitstatus` to a failure on a genuine leak (pinned by a\n      test), and `make lint` / `make typecheck` pass.","id":"938d-d6e9-2580-4faa","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Session porcelain backstop asserts a test made the change"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787297586258424001,"uuid":"34fb9e36-7549-48ca-ad11-1acc8000a016"}